WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.880
We never thought this day would actually&nbsp;
come, but Lucifer, a fan-favorite series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.480
that had escaped certain death twice, has signed&nbsp;
off for good with Season 6. The creative dramedy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:16.400
about Lucifer Morningstar abandoning hell for&nbsp;
Los Angeles premiered in 2016 on Fox. It ran&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.960
for three seasons before it was canceled.
Netflix quickly stepped in to save the show&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:25.840
for Season 4. Although the super-sized fifth&nbsp;
season was supposed to be the show's swan song,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:30.800
the streamer surprised everyone by renewing&nbsp;
Lucifer for a sixth season, which debuted in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:36.080
September with 10 episodes. Among its highlights,&nbsp;
the final season explores Lucifer's life as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:41.440
parent and brings back some familiar faces,&nbsp;
like Officer Diggs from the series' pilot.&nbsp;

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.680
But there was one important character who didn't&nbsp;
get as much screen time as they had in previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:48.134
seasons: Chloe's daughter, Trixie.

00:00:48.134 --> 00:00:53.360
"My name's Beatrice, but everybody calls me Trixie."
"That's a hooker's name."&nbsp;

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:55.760
"What's a hooker?"
"Ask your mother."&nbsp;

00:00:56.320 --> 00:01:02.000
While Trixie was never a major player on Lucifer,&nbsp;
she was central to both Chloe and Lucifer's lives.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.200
Trixie enjoyed a close relationship with Lucifer&nbsp;
over the years. But, in Season 6, she was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:12.640
relegated to attending science camp. The series&nbsp;
instead focused on the arrival of Lucifer and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:18.320
Chloe's daughter, Rory. Rory traveled back in time&nbsp;
from the future to meet the father she never knew.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.640
As such, Trixie appeared sporadically,&nbsp;
and her time on screen mostly focused on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:27.440
mourning the death of her father. So, where&nbsp;
was Trixie for the majority of the season?&nbsp;

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:31.760
When Netflix renewed Lucifer for what was&nbsp;
believed, at the time, to be its last season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.960
Scarlett Estevez began booking new roles and&nbsp;
ostensibly planning for life after the show.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:42.080
Estevez joined the fourth season of the Disney&nbsp;
Channel series Bunk'd in 2019, which may have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:46.320
been a cause for concern amongst the fans&nbsp;
looking forward to the character's return.&nbsp;

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:50.240
"I'm Parker, I've heard so much about you, and&nbsp;quite
frankly I'm a little frightened.”&nbsp;

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:54.276
“Aw, thank you."

00:01:54.497 --> 00:01:56.800
In February 2021, co-showrunners&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:01.520
Joe Henderson and Ildy Modrovich assured fans&nbsp;
that they would still see Trixie in the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:08.080
half of Season 5 and Season 6. They explained:
"[In] both Season 5B and Season 6, fans will still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.480
definitely get their Trixie fix. We adore&nbsp;
Scarlett and shuffled things around a bit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:15.840
to make sure we could keep the tale of&nbsp;
the future President of Mars going!"&nbsp;

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:19.840
The shuffling occurred because Estevez had&nbsp;
also booked a Christmas movie for Disney&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:25.360
titled Christmas Again. Filming occurred at the&nbsp;
end of 2020, which overlapped with production&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.360 --> 00:02:31.040
on Season 6 of Lucifer. But that wasn't the&nbsp;
13-year-old actress' only other work commitment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:35.200
She had also landed a lead role in an&nbsp;
upcoming Disney Channel original series.&nbsp;

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.120
It seems that Estevez's smaller presence&nbsp;
in the final season was the unfortunate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:44.000
result of scheduling conflicts. That's a shame&nbsp;
considering how much fun it sounds like Estevez&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.720
had on the set of Lucifer. Scarlett Estevez&nbsp;
is still a young talent, but she is already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:54.000
a pro at doing interviews. In the past, she has&nbsp;
spoken about her experiences filming "Lucifer"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.800
and based on what she's had to say, it sounds&nbsp;
like she had a blast working with her co-stars.&nbsp;

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.320
While speaking with Daily Dead,&nbsp;
Estevez was asked about Tom Ellis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:08.560
and Lesley-Ann Brandt. Her response was glowing:
"Tom is awesome! He has daughters, so he is really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:13.680
good with kids. Lucifer doesn't really enjoy being&nbsp;
around Trixie, but I would say in real life he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:18.880
happy when I'm around. [And] Lesley-Ann is the&nbsp;
best. We have a really great relationship offset.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.840
We've gotten together on days we aren't filming a&nbsp;
couple times, and I really love being around her."&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.160
And it's not just her fellow cast members&nbsp;
who Estevez loved working with. On Twitter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:33.200
the series' showrunner Ildy Modrovich posted&nbsp;
a behind-the-scenes pic of herself and Estevez&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:35.280
with the caption:
"[Scarlett Estevez]&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:40.000
is truly an angel in this earth."
Estevez responded with her own tweet, writing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.560
quote, "Love this!! Sending you a big hug."
It looks like even though her screen time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:49.840
in the final season ended up being limited,&nbsp;
Estevez enjoyed her stint on the show. Luckily,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:55.280
fans looking to revisit the character on Lucifer&nbsp;
can now stream all six seasons on Netflix.

